<title>ITALY: Italy's Sirti 1996 profit falls, div same.</title>
<headline>Italy's Sirti 1996 profit falls, div same.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			157.7    vs 214</p>
<p>    Ord div				  520 lire vs same</p>
<p>    Cons revenue			 1,657	up six pct</p>
<p>    Parent co net profit		 147	vs 175</p>
<p>    Financial income			98	vs 110</p>
<p>    Net financial resources	    759.2    vs 990</p>
<p>Note - Sirti Spa, a cable-laying company controlled by state telecoms holding Stet, said in a statement after a board meeting that the fall in profits was due to a lower price trend because of increasingly fierce competition.</p>
<p>--Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
